Q: Making a math game for my kids; how do I switch images based on their selection? A: <p>You can create a <strong>Map</strong>(technically speaking an <em>Object</em>) for holding/storing the image path and then manipulate it to fetch the correct <code>src</code>,</p>

<pre><code>var mapOfSource = {};
mapOfSource['key1'] = 'src1';
mapOfSource['key2'] = 'src2';
</code></pre>

<p>And, On change event of select you can fetch the data from map by simply using,</p>

<pre><code> img.src=mapOfSource['key1']
</code></pre>

<p>For Other Alternatives see this <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/4246980/how-to-create-a-simple-map-using-javascript-jquery">Q/A</a>.</p>
